From: NotaTV
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vc4: hdmi: a sink that answers on DDC is connected, also with hot-plug low

Some TVs hold hot-plug low on their input while they are on and showing it:
a TCL TV ("Beyond TV", HDMI 2) raises it only in standby. The EDID answers
on DDC and the TV shows what it gets, but the connector was "disconnected",
so userspace showed nothing (tvshell 1.0.28+ goes headless). When hot-plug
is low, probe DDC (drm_probe_ddc, one byte at 0x50): an answer means a sink
is there; with nothing plugged in the read is not acknowledged. Unlike
force_hotplug the hot-plug interrupt still works, so a TV that wakes up gets
its link retrained. vc4.notatv_ddc_detect=0 turns it off.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
@@ -132,6 +132,20 @@ static bool notatv_y420 = true;
 module_param(notatv_y420, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(notatv_y420, "Send packed 1920x2160 modes as 4K YCbCr 4:2:0 (NotaTV)");
 
+/*
+ * NotaTV: some TVs hold hot-plug low on their input while they are on and
+ * showing it - a TCL TV ("Beyond TV", HDMI 2) raises it only in standby.
+ * The EDID still answers on DDC and the TV shows what it gets (up to
+ * 340 MHz; its SCDC stays reset), but with hot-plug alone the box saw no TV
+ * and showed nothing. A sink whose EDID answers on DDC is connected; with
+ * nothing plugged in the read is not acknowledged. force_hotplug did the
+ * same but also ignores the hot-plug interrupt, so a TV that wakes up got no
+ * link retraining (vc4_hdmi_reset_link).
+ */
+static bool notatv_ddc_detect = true;
+module_param(notatv_ddc_detect, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(notatv_ddc_detect, "Treat a sink that answers on DDC as connected even with hot-plug low (NotaTV)");
+
 static u8 notatv_y420_vic_for(struct vc4_hdmi *vc4_hdmi,
 			      const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
 {
@@ -544,6 +558,10 @@ static int vc4_hdmi_connector_detect_ctx(struct drm_connector *connector,
 			status = connector_status_connected;
 	}
 
+	if (status == connector_status_disconnected && notatv_ddc_detect &&
+	    drm_probe_ddc(vc4_hdmi->ddc))
+		status = connector_status_connected;
+
 	vc4_hdmi_handle_hotplug(vc4_hdmi, ctx, status);
 	pm_runtime_put(&vc4_hdmi->pdev->dev);
 
